# Ask before any data write — Calling CRM

Do **not** insert, update, delete, seed, import, or create dummy/test records unless the user has **explicitly said yes** in this conversation. Silence, “verify the feature,” or mandatory-testing is **not** permission.

## Stop and ask first

- Mongo writes on any database: local `calling_crm`, Atlas via `deploy/.env`, or any other `MONGO_URL`
- Seed, cutover `--apply`, CSV/API import, dummy users/leads/clients, or `TEST_*` records
- **pytest** or any script that writes to the database
- Browser or API flows that create, update, or delete real records

Wait for a clear yes (e.g. “run pytest”, “apply cutover”, “create test leads”). Then do only what was approved.

## Allowed without asking

- Read-only inspection (`GET`, Mongo find, logs)
- Editing source or test **code** (do not execute anything that writes data)
- Frontend RTL tests (`yarn test`) that mock the API and do not hit Mongo

## Interaction with mandatory testing

Write or update pytest files as required. **Ask before running backend pytest.** Do not run it because verification “needs it.” Report that pytest is waiting on permission.

## Examples

```text
# BAD — unsolicited dummy lead for browser QA
POST /api/leads  {"name": "TEST_AutoConv", ...}

# BAD — pytest or cutover because the task says verify
pytest tests/backend_test.py
python scripts/local/cutover_import_leads.py --apply

# GOOD — ask, then wait
"Backend pytest will write tagged leads to local Mongo. Run it?"
```
